nancial markets and risk management.\n\nInternship Details\n\n• Duration: 6 Months\n• Work Mode: Remote\n• Stipend: ₹40,000–₹80,000 per month\n• Full-Time PPO based on performance.","requirements":"Included in Description","salary_range":null,"employment_type":"Intern","responsibilities":null,"experience_required":null},{"id":"4232fe26-e89c-4de4-a1be-a121d4484168","title":"Software Development Engineer (SDE) Intern – Backend & Distributed Systems","status":"Published","location":"Remote","created_at":"2026-07-21T17:21:57.808541+00:00","created_by":null,"department":"Information Technology (IT)","is_deleted":false,"updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:22:34.745578+00:00","description":"We are looking for exceptional Software Development Engineer (SDE) Interns to join our Core Engineering team. This internship is designed for students with strong software engineering fundamentals and prior experience building scalable production-grade systems.\n\nYou will work alongside senior engineers on high-scale backend services, cloud-native applications, distributed systems, and AI-powered infrastructure.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n• Design and implement scalable microservices handling millions of requests daily.\n• Build high-performance REST and GraphQL APIs.\n• Design distributed systems with fault tolerance and high availability.\n• Optimize backend performance using profiling and caching techniques.\n• Write production-quality code with comprehensive unit and integration tests.\n• Participate in architecture reviews and technical design discussions.\n• Deploy applications using CI/CD pipelines on cloud infrastructure.\n• Build observability dashboards using logging, metrics, and tracing.\n\nRequired Skills\n\n• Strong knowledge of Data Structures & Algorithms with competitive programming experience (Codeforces Specialist/LeetCode 500+ solved preferred).\n• Excellent knowledge of Java or Go for backend development.\n• Strong understanding of Operating Systems, Computer Networks, Database Internals, and Object-Oriented Design.\n• Experience building distributed systems.\n• Hands-on experience with Docker and Kubernetes.\n• Experience deploying applications on AWS, Azure, or GCP.\n• Strong SQL optimization skills.\n• Experience with Redis, Kafka, RabbitMQ, or other messaging systems.\n• Experience designing scalable REST and GraphQL APIs.\n• Knowledge of authentication protocols including OAuth2, JWT, OpenID Connect, and RBAC.\n• Experience writing unit tests using JUnit, PyTest, or Jest.\n• Familiarity with CI/CD using GitHub Actions, Jenkins, or GitLab CI.\n• Experience with Infrastructure as Code (Terraform or Pulumi).\n• Knowledge of monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana.\n• Familiarity with Elasticsearch/OpenSearch.\n• Understanding of software design patterns and SOLID principles.\n• Strong Git workflow experience including rebasing, pull requests, and code reviews.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• Previous internship at a product-based company.\n• Contributions to open-source projects.\n• Experience with Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), vector databases, and AI agents.\n• Experience with event-driven architectures.\n• Knowledge of gRPC and Protocol Buffers.\n• Familiarity with Apache Spark or distributed data processing frameworks.\n• Published technical blogs or conference presentations.\n• Experience building applications serving over 100K+ users.\n\nMinimum Qualification\n\n• CGPA: 8.8+\n• Strong academic record.\n• Excellent communication and problem-solving skills.\n\nInternship Details\n\n• Duration: 6 Months\n• Work Mode: Remote\n• Stipend: ₹60,000–₹1,00,000 per month\n• Full-Time PPO based on performance.","requirements":"Included in Description","salary_range":null,"employment_type":"Intern","responsibilities":null,"experience_required":null},{"id":"180f962c-acfe-4a92-989b-09c4d1635b54","title":"DATABASE ENGINEERING INTERN","status":"Published","location":"Remote","created_at":"2026-07-19T10:2